{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And spoke with Moses.</b> Like ״וּמְדַבֵּר עִם מֹשֶׁה״; its Targum is ״וּמִתְמַלֵּל עִם מֹשֶׁה״ — that is the glory of the Shechinah, as in ״וַיִּשְׁמַע אֶת הַקּוֹל מִדַּבֵּר אֵלָיו״ (Numbers 7), and He does not call it מְדַבֵּר אֵלָיו; when He calls it מִדַּבֵּר, its meaning is that the Voice speaks between Him and Himself, and the ordinary person hears from it — whereas when He calls it מְדַבֵּר, it implies that the King is speaking with the ordinary person."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:21.155087518Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}